formatted_question:
According to the paper "The Era of 1-bit LLMs: All Large Language Models are in 1.58 Bits", in the discussion of why \text{BitNet b1.58} becomes increasingly more energy efficient than the FP16 \text{LLaMA LLM} baseline as model size scales, what grows with the model size?
(A) the proportion of FP16 multiplication
(B) the percentage of \emph{nn.Linear}
(C) the size of the KV cache during inference
(D) the memory proportion of the embedding layer
(E) the time cost for \emph{nn.Linear}

